This flavor adds no files to the guest's filesystem today, and the directory has
to exist anyway: BR2_ROOTFS_OVERLAY names it, and rsync fails on a path that is
not there.

Git does not track empty directories, so without this file the directory is
absent from a fresh checkout and every image build fails with

    rsync: change_dir ".../image/flavors/base/overlay" failed: No such file or directory

which is exactly what happened when P6-9 moved the last file out of here — the
guest's os-release, which is generated now. It passed locally, where the empty
directory still existed, and failed on CI's clean checkout.

`.empty` rather than `.gitkeep` because Buildroot's own overlay rsync excludes
this name (`--exclude .empty` in system/system.mk), so the file keeps the
directory in git without landing in anybody's guest.
